Repair only the supplied scientific or grammatical issues. Return {sections:[{id:number,patches:[{before:string,after:string,issueIndex:number}],reason:string}]}. Include each supplied section exactly once. Use exact unique substrings in its candidate. At most 3 non-overlapping patches per section; their combined BEFORE text must cover at most 35% of that section. issueIndex refers to that section's issues. Keep wording elsewhere unchanged. Restore the original meaning, uncertainty and proposal status. No extra style pass. If bounded repairs cannot solve the issues, return patches:[] and explain.
INPUT DATA:
{"sections": [{"id": 2, "heading": "Related Work", "original": "The catalogue brief limits the writer to two supplied records: the entry and its curator note [S1]. The evaluation brief identifies three kinds of uncertainty that must remain visible [S2]. We will treat those qualifications as part of the content. They will not be counted as unnecessary hedging when an editor assesses whether a revision is more concise.", "candidate": "The catalogue brief restricts the writer to using only the entry and its curator note [S1]. The evaluation brief specifies that three types of uncertainty—uncertain dates, disputed locations, and unknown makers—must remain visible [S2]. We will consider these qualifications as integral content and not count them as unnecessary hedging when assessing conciseness.", "issues": [{"originalQuote": "They will not be counted as unnecessary hedging when an editor assesses whether a revision is more concise.", "revisedQuote": "We will consider these qualifications as integral content and not count them as unnecessary hedging when assessing conciseness.", "problem": "The revision removes the explicit role of an editor in assessing conciseness and instead assigns the assessment to the authors. Preserve the specified assessor."}]}], "sources": [{"id": "S1", "title": "Controlled source packet: domain and evidence brief", "excerpt": "The museum task uses catalogue entries for objects whose maker is sometimes unknown. An approximate date must remain approximate. A missing maker field is not evidence that an object was produced anonymously. Descriptions may use only the supplied catalogue entry and curator note.", "content_kind": "author_constructed_evaluation_fixture"}, {"id": "S2", "title": "Controlled source packet: experimental design brief", "excerpt": "The proposed sample contains 28 objects. A concise description will be compared with the original catalogue prose. The study will measure readability and whether uncertain dates, disputed locations and unknown makers are preserved. No new provenance research will be conducted.", "content_kind": "author_constructed_evaluation_fixture"}]}
